<p>Canadian authorities are investigating after two people fired multiple shots at the U.S. consulate in downtown Toronto at about 4:30 a.m. on March 10, then fled in a white SUV; police reported no injuries. Toronto police and the Royal Canadian Mounted Police are treating the case as a national security incident, and officers have been searching for the suspects. Canada has moved to increase security at U.S. and Israeli diplomatic sites in Toronto and at embassies in Ottawa. Officials linked the step to heightened concern after recent gunfire incidents at synagogues in the Toronto area. The motive remains unclear. Ontario’s premier suggested a possible connection to the Iran war, but reporting stressed investigators are still working to determine whether any link exists.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Ddi3w4V1NIp1TCVBwGvbHhvFp3BaTp5HE1HsCYTcHiip-ztS-ZT7ZNavS8M5XYcTFiEvyBhBqjqJnGJGEj1GnuGWf_Q66CCoyV6_3kKjD5LYBqxn_DB0I9yxKDvGL13DvT_JanME2LedDo0rQNVU_EPoRuH0VrNvsRU_AcJ9M7T4DYL1QMbvmROQ5gtKSplV97iPHK_YHXdplHrueA4xVZlXHNB_8rhmAcF0c04uM6jwjj5U8SnegWQ0w6SZCX1HKVjOPfkgvw' alt='Police investigate after gunfire struck the U.S. consulate in Toronto.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Weapon detail: Police said both suspects used a single handgun to shoot at the building before fleeing.</li><li>Police briefing: Toronto Police Deputy Chief Frank Barredo said the suspects got out of their vehicle and fired multiple shots at the consulate before escaping.</li><li>Getaway vehicle: Police described the suspects’ vehicle as a white Honda CRV SUV.</li><li>National security lead: RCMP Chief Superintendent Chris Leather said investigators are treating the shooting as a national security matter and that the RCMP is working with Toronto police to understand the motive.</li><li>Public assistance: Police asked anyone with information to help identify the suspects and locate the white SUV used in the escape.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Toronto Police Service: Police said two people got out of a white SUV around 4:30 a.m., fired multiple shots at the building, and fled. No injuries were reported. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/canadian-police-investigate-gunfire-at-us-consulate-in-toronto/article70728240.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Royal Canadian Mounted Police: The RCMP called it a national security incident and said it was coordinating with Toronto police while boosting security at U.S. and Israeli diplomatic sites and embassies in Ottawa. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346145/shots-fired-us-consulate-toronto-canada-premier-hints-iran-war-link'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Ontario government: Ontario’s premier suggested the shooting could be linked to the Iran war, while the investigation continues. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346145/shots-fired-us-consulate-toronto-canada-premier-hints-iran-war-link'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Canadian security context: Officials said the shooting followed gunfire incidents at synagogues in the Toronto area, adding to concerns about threats around community and diplomatic sites. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/toronto-police-say-shots-fired-at-us-consulate-no-injuries-reported'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/canadian-police-investigate-gunfire-at-us-consulate-in-toronto/article70728240.ece'>Canadian police investigate gunfire at U.S. consulate in Toronto</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/toronto-police-say-shots-fired-at-us-consulate-no-injuries-reported'>Canada boosts security at US, Israeli diplomatic buildings after consulate shooting</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346145/shots-fired-us-consulate-toronto-canada-premier-hints-iran-war-link'>Sh